    <h2>Confidentiality in therapy</h2>
    <p>What you tell your therapist stays between you and Balm. We do not share it with family, employers, schools or churches without your permission.</p>
    <p>There are a few situations where we may need to share information without your permission:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>if we believe you or someone else is at serious risk of harm</li>
      <li>if a child or vulnerable adult may be in danger</li>
      <li>if a court or the law requires it</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Where we can, we will talk with you first. Our clinicians may discuss cases in supervision to keep care safe, without using your name.</p>

    <h2>Children and teenagers</h2>
    <p>We share the themes we notice with parents and carers, and how they can help. The details of what a child says or plays stay private, unless we are worried about their safety.</p>

    <h2>What our website forms collect</h2>
    <p>Our forms ask only for your name, contact details, who the help is for and a good time to call. Please don't include medical details. Form messages are sent by email to our intake team through a service called Web3Forms, and we delete them from our inbox after [period] once you are booked or no longer need us.</p>

    <h2>WhatsApp and email</h2>
    <p>WhatsApp messages are encrypted between your phone and ours. Email is less secure, so please keep sensitive details for your session.</p>

    <h2>Website analytics</h2>
    <p>We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits. It does not use cookies or track you across other websites.</p>

    <h2>Your records</h2>
    <p>Clinical records are kept securely [describe storage] for [period], as required by [professional or legal standard]. You can ask to see the information we hold about you.</p>

